1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,255
This walkthrough shows Nirob version three point three, a local
personal finance prototype.

2
00:00:06,255 --> 00:00:09,004
All balances and payments are synthetic.

3
00:00:09,004 --> 00:00:13,609
The recording uses a separate demo workspace and a virtual passkey.

4
00:00:13,609 --> 00:00:16,564
Your saved personal workspace is untouched.

5
00:00:16,564 --> 00:00:20,276
Model waiting time is shortened in the edited footage.

6
00:00:21,776 --> 00:00:26,932
Open the complete Nirob Agent folder and double click START NIROB dot
cmd.

7
00:00:26,932 --> 00:00:29,022
Keep the launcher window open.

8
00:00:29,022 --> 00:00:33,621
Wait for the browser to open localhost, port four one seven seven.

9
00:00:33,621 --> 00:00:36,966
The full folder needs Node twenty four or later.

10
00:00:36,966 --> 00:00:40,938
A source ZIP also needs its dependencies and model files.

11
00:00:40,938 --> 00:00:44,631
PDF reading needs Python and the listed requirements.

12
00:00:46,131 --> 00:00:48,347
Choose Register your passkey.

13
00:00:48,347 --> 00:00:54,841
On your computer, the browser and Windows may offer fingerprint, face,
or device PIN.

14
00:00:54,841 --> 00:00:59,272
Nirob receives a signed response, never a biometric image.

15
00:00:59,272 --> 00:01:06,530
This recording uses a virtual authenticator, so it does not show a
physical fingerprint prompt.

16
00:01:06,530 --> 00:01:09,891
On later visits, choose Unlock with passkey.

17
00:01:11,391 --> 00:01:15,793
Open Agent workspace and type your question into the chat box.

18
00:01:15,793 --> 00:01:25,803
Here, we ask for a business idea based on recorded spending, with
maths tutoring skills, three hours a week, and a two thousand taka
ceiling.

19
00:01:25,803 --> 00:01:30,630
The local Qwen three, four billion parameter model produces a reply.

20
00:01:30,630 --> 00:01:34,677
Read its assumptions and check suggestions before acting.

21
00:01:36,177 --> 00:01:39,534
Expand Financial context used beneath the reply.

22
00:01:39,534 --> 00:01:47,018
This demo contains seven complete synthetic months, March through
September, plus the current month so far.

23
00:01:47,018 --> 00:01:50,585
Check income, spending, and net recorded cash flow.

24
00:01:50,585 --> 00:01:55,341
Missing cash purchases or future commitments can change the picture.

25
00:01:55,341 --> 00:01:59,887
The current partial month is not a complete month for comparison.

26
00:02:01,387 --> 00:02:04,394
Ask a follow-up in the same conversation.

27
00:02:04,394 --> 00:02:08,353
Here, we request a first-week plan within three hours.

28
00:02:08,353 --> 00:02:12,606
Nirob uses recent messages and recorded financial context.

29
00:02:12,606 --> 00:02:16,639
This is in-context coaching, not a newly trained model.

30
00:02:16,639 --> 00:02:24,412
Check that the suggested activities fit your own skills and situation;
an idea is not a promise of income.

31
00:02:25,912 --> 00:02:27,649
Open Budget and advisor.

32
00:02:27,649 --> 00:02:31,991
Enter a savings goal and your skills, then request a budget.

33
00:02:31,991 --> 00:02:36,839
The app calculates from recorded income, expenses and unpaid bills.

34
00:02:36,839 --> 00:02:39,371
Review any shortfall before saving.

35
00:02:39,371 --> 00:02:47,693
A saved budget is a plan for the demo; it does not move money or
guarantee that unrecorded costs have been covered.

36
00:02:49,193 --> 00:02:54,043
Open Bills and approvals and upload the included sample bill image.

37
00:02:54,043 --> 00:02:56,432
The app extracts readable fields.

38
00:02:56,432 --> 00:03:00,920
Check the payee, amount, reference and due date before saving.

39
00:03:00,920 --> 00:03:06,494
English image OCR and PDF extraction are supported, but recognition
can fail.

40
00:03:06,494 --> 00:03:14,168
The clean sample used here does not establish accuracy on handwriting,
Bengali bills or noisy photographs.

41
00:03:15,668 --> 00:03:19,410
Start a chat and ask, Send five hundred to Rahim.

42
00:03:19,410 --> 00:03:22,159
The app prepares a draft for review.

43
00:03:22,159 --> 00:03:29,491
An explicit amount and recipient are required; incomplete requests
should ask for clarification.

44
00:03:29,491 --> 00:03:32,316
The AI has no payment execution tool.

45
00:03:32,316 --> 00:03:38,578
A known saved bill can also be requested by name, such as Pay my
electricity bill.

46
00:03:40,078 --> 00:03:41,813
Open Bills and approvals.

47
00:03:41,813 --> 00:03:44,310
Compare the draft with your request.

48
00:03:44,310 --> 00:03:49,859
Correct, incorrect, and unsafe draft feedback is separate from payment
approval.

49
00:03:49,859 --> 00:03:56,450
Choose Review and approve, inspect the exact amount and recipient,
then Verify passkey and pay.

50
00:03:56,450 --> 00:04:04,288
The server verifies a fresh challenge bound to this transaction before
posting the simulated payment to Activity.

51
00:04:05,788 --> 00:04:11,063
Open Activity and enter a cash purchase with its description, amount
and category.

52
00:04:11,063 --> 00:04:15,052
This makes the purchase available to the monthly calculations.

53
00:04:15,052 --> 00:04:17,625
These are manually entered demo records.

54
00:04:17,625 --> 00:04:26,824
Nirob does not automatically receive real card transactions or
intercept a Visa request simply because an account or card is listed
in the app.

55
00:04:28,324 --> 00:04:32,134
In Safety and trust, generate an unknown demo request.

56
00:04:32,134 --> 00:04:35,168
Inspect the alert and choose Block request.

57
00:04:35,168 --> 00:04:39,895
This demonstrates the app holding and blocking a simulated request.

58
00:04:39,895 --> 00:04:42,717
It does not monitor a real bank account.

59
00:04:42,717 --> 00:04:51,254
Flagged approvals require two distinct registered passkeys, which do
not necessarily mean two different physical devices.

60
00:04:52,754 --> 00:05:04,960
The automated review card shows one hundred passing development
scenarios and a Wilson lower bound of ninety six point three percent,
against the unchanged ninety five percent requirement.

61
00:05:04,960 --> 00:05:10,673
Eighty cases invoked the model; twenty checked clarification or policy
before inference.

62
00:05:10,673 --> 00:05:13,659
Personal bill and transfer trust are separate.

63
00:05:13,659 --> 00:05:18,529
Automated results never grant your personal trust or bypass final
approval.

64
00:05:20,029 --> 00:05:23,720
Open Settings and data, or click the bottom-left name.

65
00:05:23,720 --> 00:05:27,957
Replace My workspace with your own label and choose Save name.

66
00:05:27,957 --> 00:05:32,332
The previous fixed MIST label has been removed from the product.

67
00:05:32,332 --> 00:05:35,749
The new name is saved for this local installation.

68
00:05:35,749 --> 00:05:38,825
The application itself is still called Nirob.

69
00:05:40,325 --> 00:05:49,722
In Settings and data, choose income or spending, select an active demo
account, and enter the amount, description, category and date.

70
00:05:49,722 --> 00:05:53,538
Earlier dates let you create your own monthly history.

71
00:05:53,538 --> 00:05:58,555
If the workspace is empty, add a synthetic source under Accounts
first.

72
00:05:58,555 --> 00:06:03,430
These entries are bookkeeping records, not live banking transactions.

73
00:06:04,930 --> 00:06:11,270
Download the example JSON file and edit its sample accounts,
transactions and bills.

74
00:06:11,270 --> 00:06:15,724
Select your file and preview the counts, months and totals.

75
00:06:15,724 --> 00:06:20,856
Review replacement, type REPLACE DEMO DATA, and verify your passkey.

76
00:06:20,856 --> 00:06:28,630
Import replaces the dataset and resets personal trust while keeping
your name and passkey registration.

77
00:06:28,630 --> 00:06:30,970
Unlock again after replacement.

78
00:06:32,470 --> 00:06:41,696
Clear demo records keeps your workspace name and passkey, while
removing financial records, chats, feedback and old audit history.

79
00:06:41,696 --> 00:06:47,232
Reset entire workspace also removes the profile and app passkey
registrations.

80
00:06:47,232 --> 00:06:52,555
Each action needs its exact confirmation phrase and fresh passkey
approval.

81
00:06:52,555 --> 00:06:57,168
Separate exports, backups and authenticator-held passkeys remain.

82
00:06:57,168 --> 00:07:01,284
The reset shown here affects only our recording workspace.

83
00:07:02,784 --> 00:07:10,734
You can now name the workspace, add your own demo data, chat about
goals, prepare payments and review the evidence.

84
00:07:10,734 --> 00:07:13,776
Every final payment still requires approval.

85
00:07:13,776 --> 00:07:16,886
The current prototype has no bank connection.

86
00:07:16,886 --> 00:07:20,758
Keep private data folders out of shared source packages.

87
00:07:20,758 --> 00:07:24,560
Close the launcher when you finish using the local app.
